  "releaseNotes": "10.3.2\n\n* Fixed: ShellExt.RunCommandWithResultAsync (and so RunCommandAsync and the PDF conversion built\n  on it) started the command even when the cancellation token was already cancelled, and a fast\n  command could finish before the cancellation was noticed, so the call returned normally instead\n  of throwing. An already-cancelled token now throws OperationCanceledException before anything\n  is started.\n\nUpgrading from an earlier version? 10.3.1 changed what IOExtensions.UnifyPathSeperator does with\na leading // or \\\\ on Windows, and 10.3.0 changed how Com.H.Shell and Com.H.Pdf behave. Their\nnotes list every change:\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H/10.3.1#releasenotes-body-tab\nhttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Com.H/10.3.0#releasenotes-body-tab",
